{
  "id": "kerr-cavity-quadratures-third-science",
  "name": "Homogeneous driven Kerr cavity and optical bistability",
  "description": "Complex cavity amplitude has intensity-dependent phase detuning; two quadratures retain optical bistability. No spatial modulation, frequency combs, solitons or full dispersive LLE simulation. Illustrative normalized loss1,detuning2,Kerr coefficient1,real drive1.4,initial field0; horizon50,RK4step0.01. Spatial derivatives are zero by the stated homogeneous specialization. https://bpb-us-e1.wpmucdn.com/blog.umd.edu/dist/3/661/files/2019/07/2014_PRA_Stability_Analysis_LLE.pdf Original mathematical transcription/adaptation; not a calibrated forecast. Signed net-rate flows implement the stated equations. No numerical clamps or hidden resets.",
  "category": "physics",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.89.063814",
  "reference": "Godey, Balakireva, Coillet and Chembo (2014), Stability analysis of the spatiotemporal Lugiato-Lefever model, Phys Rev A89:063814, homogeneous specialization of Eq4.",
